course: dictionary
lesson: 13508
title: Immobilise: stopping things from moving
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Immobilise means to stop something from moving or working. Its parts give a clue: "im-" means not, and "mobile" means able to move. «The nurse used a sling to immobilise Sam's broken arm.» The sling keeps the arm still.
explain: Context gives you more clues. «The spider's venom immobilised the fly, so it could not escape.» The fly stopped moving because of the venom, so immobilised must mean stopped from moving. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "the venom stopped the fly" still makes sense.
explain: The word also means stopping a car from being started. «The police put a wheel clamp on the car to immobilise it.» Cars have immobilisers that stop thieves starting them. The same idea runs through every use: something cannot move or work.
fact: Immobilise means to stop someone or something from moving or working.
fact: In first aid, you immobilise an injury with a splint or sling so that it does not get worse.
fact: To immobilise a car means to stop it being started, for example with a car alarm or wheel clamp.
fact: «Immobilise» can be spelt «immobilize» in American English.
fact: Useful phrases: immobilise the injury, immobilise the prey, immobilise a car.
exercise: «The sling was used to immobilise Sam's arm.» What does immobilise mean here? | To wash the arm | To cover the arm in paint | *To keep the arm still | To make the arm bigger
exercise: «The spider's venom immobilised the fly.» What did the venom do to the fly? | *It stopped the fly from moving | It made the fly fly faster | It made the fly hungry | It made the fly sing
exercise: Which word means the same as immobilise in «The wheel clamp will immobilise the car»? | Start | *Stop | Wash | Paint
test: Why does a doctor immobilise an injured arm? | To keep the arm cold | To make the arm dance | *To stop the arm getting worse | To make the arm longer
test: Which word fits the gap? A sling is used to ___ a broken arm. | *immobilise | celebrate | sing | dance
exam: Which word is the American spelling of immobilise? | *immobilize | immobilyse | immobilice | immobilese
